**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** The Experiments bay shows and builds v2: the scan's axes and blocks, the edited experiment's role, session and notes, and each row's name, role and data badge (the S9.1 brief: the Experiments bay reads v2; 001 §O 'Automation: every new control gets a stable id'; .spec-md §4 UI: the bay stays domain-free and the button and the test send the same message). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`: (a) `ExperimentRoleMark` = `RoleChosen` | `RoleNotChosen` and `ExperimentRoleOption = { key : ConstructorUiKey; caption : ControlCaption; mark : ExperimentRoleMark }`, one role box. (b) `ExperimentRow` (`ExperimentControls.fs:ExperimentRow`) gains `badge : ControlCaption`, the data badge's text, after `description`. (c) `ExperimentControlsState` (`ExperimentControls.fs:ExperimentControlsState`) gains `scanLines : ControlCaption list` (the closed blocks and the current block's held axes), `scanAvailability : ControlAvailability` (Add variable and Add block), `roleOptions : ExperimentRoleOption list`, `sessionText : ControlCaption`, `notesText : ControlCaption` and `bookkeepingAvailability : ControlAvailability` (present while an experiment is loaded in a writable kit), each empty or withheld in `emptyExperimentControls`. `ExperimentControlsHandlers` (`ExperimentControls.fs:ExperimentControlsHandlers`) gains `addScanAxis : unit -> unit`, `addScanBlock : unit -> unit`, `setRole : ConstructorUiKey -> unit`, `setSession : ControlCaption -> unit` and `setNotes : ControlCaption -> unit`. (d) The view: under the range rows, the scan lines (a `TextBlock` per line in the panel `experimentScanSummary`) and the two buttons `Add variable` and `Add block`, beside Add and New in the box look `actionButton` draws; while `bookkeepingAvailability` is present, a role row of the seven boxes (`optionBoxV`, the chosen one in the chosen colour), a `Session:` field and a `Notes:` field committing on Enter and on losing focus as `numberField` does; each collection row shows its badge text beside its description. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: `experimentScanSummary` (`ExperimentScanSummary`), `experimentAddScanAxisButton` (`ExperimentAddScanAxisButton`), `experimentAddScanBlockButton` (`ExperimentAddScanBlockButton`), `experimentRoleChoice (role : ConstructorUiKey)` (`ExperimentRole_<key>`), `experimentSessionField` (`ExperimentSessionField`), `experimentNotesField` (`ExperimentNotesField`) and `experimentRowBadge (experiment : ConstructorUiKey)` (`ExperimentBadge_<key>`), each a uniquely named static member. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type ExperimentRole with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`science`, `calibration`, `dark`, `drift-check`, `diagnostic`, `ignored`, `planned`) and `member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `text`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `model.experimentState` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:experimentState`) fills the fields: each closed block as `Block <k>: <its text>` and the held axes as `This block: <their describes joined by " × ">` (step 288's texts); `scanAvailability` as `addAvailability`; for the edited experiment the seven roles in tag order, its session's text (empty for none) and its notes, `bookkeepingAvailability` present only when the draft edits an experiment and the kit is writable (step 185's access); each row's `description` `<name> [<role.text>] — <description>` and `badge` `model.dataBadgeOf`'s `text` (step 295). `experimentHandlers` sends `ExpAddScanAxis`, `ExpAddScanBlock` (step 292) and, for the edited experiment's id, `SetExperimentRole` (the role whose `uiKey` is pressed), `SetExperimentSession` and `SetExperimentNotes` (step 294). No other control, option or message is added. Tests (`ExperimentControlsTests`, ui-tests unless named): `the bay's scan, role, session and notes UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the seven ids above are stable (`ExperimentScanSummary`, `ExperimentRole_calibration`, `ExperimentBadge_3`, …). `Add variable and Add block list the held axes and blocks under the range`: over the bay's model, choosing the sample's R2 and pressing `experimentAddScanAxisButton`, then the sample's R1 and `experimentAddScanBlockButton`, shows the summary lines `Block 1: …R2… × …R1…, capture …` in order, and the two buttons are withheld with nothing chosen. `an experiment loaded in the editor shows its role, session and notes, and a press on a role sends it`: with E1 committed and loaded (`ExpEdit`), the role row shows `Science` chosen, the session and notes fields are empty, and pressing `experimentRoleChoice` of `calibration` leaves E1 a `CalibrationRun` with `Calibration` chosen; with no experiment loaded the row is absent. `each collected experiment's row shows its name, its role and its data badge`: E1 committed shows a row reading `E1 [Science] — …` and the badge `no data`. ui-smoke `pressing Add variable between two axes and Add records one two-variable experiment` : pressing the sample's candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r2`, `experimentAddScanAxisButton`, the candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r1` and `experimentAddButton` records one experiment whose scan has two axes in one block. `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' handler record gains the five fields as `ignore`, every fact keeping its assertions. `ScrollExtentTests`: `Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable` also loads an experiment into the editor, so the role row, the two fields and the scan summary are in the bay it scrolls, its assertion kept. `ElementMenuTests` and `InverseConstructorTests` read `experimentState` fields that keep their meaning, and nothing in them changes.

**Acceptance.** After the bay reads v2, it MUST show the draft's scan lines with Add variable and Add block, the loaded experiment's role, session and notes sending `SetExperimentRole` / `SetExperimentSession` / `SetExperimentNotes`, and each row's name, role and data badge, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Add variable between two axes and Add records one two-variable experiment`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the bay's scan, role, session and notes UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `Add variable and Add block list the held axes and blocks under the range`, `an experiment loaded in the editor shows its role, session and notes, and a press on a role sends it` and `each collected experiment's row shows its name, its role and its data badge`, the count rising by 4, and the changed `Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
